  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463170",
      "title": "Using the Native Event Object",
      "lectureOrder": 26,
      "videoOrder": 22,
      "sourceHash": "5d4e64a51cc279418f09bec9331bc631e51f93edbe61e007260fb872ca26b04a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.11,
          "end": 3.76,
          "en": "So this is taking shape.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.76,
          "end": 8.31,
          "en": "Let's now enhanced his mini dummy app here a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.31,
          "end": 12.65,
          "en": "And let's add an input of type text here, just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.65,
          "end": 16.24,
          "en": "And below that paragraph where I say Your Name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.24,
          "end": 18.57,
          "en": "and in here, I wanna output the username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.57,
          "end": 21.4,
          "en": "But now the user should be able to enter the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.4,
          "end": 25.5,
          "en": "in this input here, that's the new thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.5,
          "end": 28.833,
          "en": "So we can have a name field here in our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.73,
          "end": 33.38,
          "en": "Initially it could be empty or your name, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.38,
          "end": 35.81,
          "en": "And we can output the name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.81,
          "end": 37.453,
          "en": "with the double curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.5,
          "end": 40.6,
          "en": "But now I also have this input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.6,
          "end": 44.03,
          "en": "and whenever I type in here, I want to update the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.03,
          "end": 46.473,
          "en": "which is output in this paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.32,
          "end": 48.823,
          "en": "Now, how could we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.33,
          "end": 53.26,
          "en": "Well, now that we learned about listening to events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.26,
          "end": 56.13,
          "en": "we should have all the tools we need for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.13,
          "end": 59.36,
          "en": "We can add an event listener with v-on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.36,
          "end": 62.27,
          "en": "and now of course, I don't wanna listen to the click event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.27,
          "end": 64.36,
          "en": "but to every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.36,
          "end": 67.17,
          "en": "We could do it as with keyup or keydown,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.17,
          "end": 70.22,
          "en": "which all have their special behaviors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.22,
          "end": 75.22,
          "en": "The best event to listen to on an input HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.65,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "is the input event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 79.82,
          "en": "Which is a default Dom event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.82,
          "end": 83.65,
          "en": "available on input elements, nothing Vue specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.65,
          "end": 85.33,
          "en": "You can listen to the input event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.33,
          "end": 87.203,
          "en": "in vanilla JavaScript as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.18,
          "end": 92.28,
          "en": "Here with v-on I'm telling Vue that I want to listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.28,
          "end": 96.27000000000001,
          "en": "to this input event on this input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.27000000000001,
          "end": 97.66,
          "en": "And there for now, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.66,
          "end": 101.02000000000001,
          "en": "we can specify to code between these double quotes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.02000000000001,
          "end": 104.33,
          "en": "that should execute when an input event is admitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.33,
          "end": 106.86,
          "en": "which will be the case on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.86,
          "end": 110.223,
          "en": "That is how the input event is emitted by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 113.35,
          "en": "So now again, we could put the code in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.35,
          "end": 116.77000000000001,
          "en": "or use this better approach of using a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.77000000000001,
          "end": 120.333,
          "en": "So I'll do that, add a little method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.333,
          "end": 122.99,
          "en": "setName could be the method name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.99,
          "end": 124.85,
          "en": "because that's what we're going to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.85,
          "end": 126.06,
          "en": "Again, the name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.06,
          "end": 127.87,
          "en": "but of course you wanna name the method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.87,
          "end": 130.49,
          "en": "such that it describes what it's going to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.49,
          "end": 131.89,
          "en": "So here I'll use setName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.25,
          "end": 135.63,
          "en": "and then I want to set this name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.63,
          "end": 140.53,
          "en": "So this name property, which we added to our data object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.53,
          "end": 143.15,
          "en": "equal to what the user entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.15,
          "end": 145.79,
          "en": "And that's going to be a bit tricky, won't it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.79,
          "end": 148.28,
          "en": "Because how do we know what the user entered?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.28,
          "end": 150.51,
          "en": "We know that the user entered something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.51,
          "end": 152.56,
          "en": "because we're listening to that event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.56,
          "end": 155.883,
          "en": "but how do we get the concrete value the user entered?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.46,
          "end": 161.68,
          "en": "While there is a built in behavior built into JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.68,
          "end": 164.57,
          "en": "not into Vue, which we can leverage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.57,
          "end": 168.44,
          "en": "First of all, we can point at the setName method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.44,
          "end": 172.41,
          "en": "which is the method we wanna execute on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.41,
          "end": 175.36,
          "en": "And now there's a cool behavior in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.36,
          "end": 179.01,
          "en": "not in Vue, Vue just also is able to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.01,
          "end": 181.34,
          "en": "When you add an event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.34,
          "end": 184.18,
          "en": "and you then point at a function that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.18,
          "end": 185.78,
          "en": "when that event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.78,
          "end": 190.68,
          "en": "That function will automatically get one argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 192.13,
          "en": "The browser will ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.13,
          "end": 194.36,
          "en": "that this argument is provided so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.36,
          "end": 196.76,
          "en": "And that will be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.76,
          "end": 199.373,
          "en": "describing the event that occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.76,
          "end": 203.51,
          "en": "So here in setName,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.51,
          "end": 207.54,
          "en": "we can accept this one argument, this one parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.54,
          "end": 209.44,
          "en": "You can name it however you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.44,
          "end": 212.223,
          "en": "but you will always get this by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.41,
          "end": 217.16,
          "en": "We would have gotten this here for add and reduce as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.16,
          "end": 218.64,
          "en": "We just overrode it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.64,
          "end": 222.53,
          "en": "with our own custom argument, we're passing in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.53,
          "end": 224.64,
          "en": "But since I'm not executing setName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.64,
          "end": 227.47,
          "en": "with parentheses here, but I am pointing edit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.47,
          "end": 228.89,
          "en": "I don't override it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.89,
          "end": 233.16,
          "en": "And I let the browser provide this default event object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.16,
          "end": 234.84,
          "en": "And why is this useful?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.84,
          "end": 237.32999999999998,
          "en": "Because this default event object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.32999999999998,
          "end": 240.25,
          "en": "will be full of information about the event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 240.25,
          "end": 242.66,
          "en": "And for example, it will give us information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.66,
          "end": 247.02,
          "en": "about the HTML element on which this event occurred,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 247.02,
          "end": 249.1,
          "en": "which is the input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 249.1,
          "end": 253.76,
          "en": "And we can then read the current value stored in this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.76,
          "end": 256.63,
          "en": "from that input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.63,
          "end": 259.46,
          "en": "And we get access to the target off the event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 259.46,
          "end": 263.12,
          "en": "with events.target and that's vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 263.12,
          "end": 264.95,
          "en": "This is nothing Vue specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 264.95,
          "end": 268.43,
          "en": "This would work in vanilla JavaScript as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 268.43,
          "end": 270.76,
          "en": "This gives us access to the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 270.76,
          "end": 272.29,
          "en": "on which the event occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.29,
          "end": 274.52,
          "en": "And this is the input element in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 274.52,
          "end": 277.02,
          "en": "which will have a value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 277.02,
          "end": 280.07,
          "en": "Again, that's just vanilla javaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.07,
          "end": 282.48,
          "en": "and you can search for MDN input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 282.48,
          "end": 286.09000000000003,
          "en": "to find more documentation on this input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.09000000000003,
          "end": 290.27,
          "en": "And in here you will eventually somewhere find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.27,
          "end": 294.04,
          "en": "that this has a value property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294.04,
          "end": 297.68,
          "en": "which you can use to read what the user entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 297.68,
          "end": 299.72,
          "en": "So this will be the value to user entered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 299.72,
          "end": 303.11,
          "en": "setName will be called on every input events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 303.11,
          "end": 306.85,
          "en": "So on every keystroke and this should update the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306.85,
          "end": 309.98,
          "en": "our data and it property here with every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 309.98,
          "end": 313.153,
          "en": "with the value to user currently entered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 314.45,
          "end": 316.6,
          "en": "And then we're outputting name down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 316.6,
          "end": 318.63,
          "en": "And if we now save that in reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 318.63,
          "end": 322.36,
          "en": "I can enter Maximilian and you see how this updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 322.36,
          "end": 323.903,
          "en": "in the paragraph below.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 325.78,
          "end": 329.04,
          "en": "And that's Vue's reactivity in action, again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 329.04,
          "end": 333.22,
          "en": "It allows us to listen to this event and execute this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 333.22,
          "end": 336.54,
          "en": "and it's then all the detects that name changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 336.54,
          "end": 339.47,
          "en": "and updates it in the places on the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 339.47,
          "end": 341.71,
          "en": "where updating is needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 341.71,
          "end": 343.12,
          "en": "And as a side note,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 343.12,
          "end": 346.05,
          "en": "if I inspect this here in the Chrome Dev Tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 346.05,
          "end": 349.9,
          "en": "there is something ever interesting which we can notice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 349.9,
          "end": 354.36,
          "en": "If you watch this part on the right here this HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 354.36,
          "end": 355.73,
          "en": "You'll see that the parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 355.73,
          "end": 359.15999999999997,
          "en": "that are rerendered the browser flash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 359.15999999999997,
          "end": 362.69,
          "en": "you see the paragraph with my name flashes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 362.69,
          "end": 364.01,
          "en": "Now you will also see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 364.01,
          "end": 366.2,
          "en": "that nothing else on the screen flashed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 366.2,
          "end": 368.3,
          "en": "For example, the counter didn't flash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 368.3,
          "end": 372.37,
          "en": "This counter only flashes. If I changed the counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 372.37,
          "end": 373.6,
          "en": "Now these are the parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 373.6,
          "end": 376.51,
          "en": "which are actually rerendered on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 376.51,
          "end": 380.71,
          "en": "And you see that only the parts that really changed in code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 380.71,
          "end": 383.94,
          "en": "are rerendered on the screen and that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 383.94,
          "end": 387.77,
          "en": "If Vue would update the entire screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 387.77,
          "end": 390.72,
          "en": "whenever something changed somewhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 390.72,
          "end": 392.713,
          "en": "this would be bad for performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 393.89,
          "end": 396.81,
          "en": "Instead Vue is really smart and it sees that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 396.81,
          "end": 399.89,
          "en": "with every keystroke here, only the name changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 399.89,
          "end": 404.05,
          "en": "And hence it only finds the places where I used the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 404.05,
          "end": 407.26,
          "en": "in this case, this paragraph and update stat",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 407.26,
          "end": 410.13,
          "en": "and the rest is well left untouched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 410.13,
          "end": 413.763,
          "en": "And hence we save performance or have a better performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 414.8,
          "end": 418.21,
          "en": "Now, this is how we can work with events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 418.21,
          "end": 422.54,
          "en": "There's just one more note about this default event object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 422.54,
          "end": 426.31,
          "en": "You could have a scenario that you need to call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 426.31,
          "end": 429.17,
          "en": "your method explicitly on your own here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 429.17,
          "end": 431.76,
          "en": "as we did it with add and reduce.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 431.76,
          "end": 432.79,
          "en": "For example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 432.79,
          "end": 436.42,
          "en": "because you need to pass in some other argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 436.42,
          "end": 439.913,
          "en": "like second name, which I always want to use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 441.88,
          "end": 446.88,
          "en": "We could accept this here, second name or last name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 447.62,
          "end": 450.73,
          "en": "and then update name with whatever the user entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 450.73,
          "end": 455.623,
          "en": "plus last name, maybe also add a white space in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 457.79,
          "end": 460.92,
          "en": "The problem with that is that we now no longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 460.92,
          "end": 465.12,
          "en": "get this default event object as a first argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 465.12,
          "end": 469.13,
          "en": "Now to still pass that in, there is a special variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 469.13,
          "end": 471.1,
          "en": "which you can use here in your template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 471.1,
          "end": 473.57,
          "en": "and that's dollar sign event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 473.57,
          "end": 477.47,
          "en": "This is a reserved name and Vue gives this variable to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 477.47,
          "end": 481.63,
          "en": "to give you access to this built in default event object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 481.63,
          "end": 484.56,
          "en": "which you get automatically by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 484.56,
          "end": 487.43,
          "en": "So that you can use it here in this code as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 487.43,
          "end": 492.05,
          "en": "And for example, still pass it in as a first argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 492.05,
          "end": 493.693,
          "en": "to setName, if you wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 494.74,
          "end": 498.35,
          "en": "So whenever you find yourself using an arguments here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 498.35,
          "end": 501.51,
          "en": "or you simply can't just point at a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 501.51,
          "end": 505.04,
          "en": "for whatever reason and you need that built in event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 505.04,
          "end": 508.19,
          "en": "you can access it with dollar sign event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 508.19,
          "end": 511.09,
          "en": "But again, this is only needed if you're not just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 511.09,
          "end": 513.97,
          "en": "pointing at the method as we did it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 513.97,
          "end": 518.3,
          "en": "Hence now if a reload, this still all works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 518.3,
          "end": 521.28,
          "en": "but now with help of dollar sign event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 521.28,
          "end": 522.86,
          "en": "That's just in our side note,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 522.86,
          "end": 526.04,
          "en": "because sometimes this is exactly what you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 526.04,
          "end": 528.67,
          "en": "to get access to both to build an event object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 528.67,
          "end": 531.94,
          "en": "you get automatically and still execute code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 531.94,
          "end": 533.46,
          "en": "on your own explicitly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 533.46,
          "end": 536.983,
          "en": "for example, to pass in your own arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
